<title>USA: Network Long Distance Q3 net loss.</title>
<headline>Network Long Distance Q3 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>BATON ROUGE, La. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months</p>
<p>						  Ended Dec. 31,</p>
<p>				   1996	  1995	  1995</p>
<p>(In Thousands)			    Restated   Not Restated</p>
<p>Billable Minutes	    83,967	69,079	48,622</p>
<p>Revenues		    $ 14,487    $ 11,439    $  7,373</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)	 $ (4,989)   $    264    $     24</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per Shr  (0.81)   $   0.05    $   0.01</p>
<p>Avg Shares Outstanding	6,141	5,119	 3,190</p>
<p>						    Nine Months</p>
<p>Billable Minutes	   260,243     201,460     144,647</p>
<p>Revenues		    $ 44,128    $ 31,251    $ 21,597</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)	 $ (4,635)   $    533    $     64</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per Shr  (0.76)   $   0.11    $   0.02</p>
<p>Avg Shares Outstanding     6,088	 5,063	 2,756</p>
<p>NOTE: The current third quarter and first nine months includes a $4.9 million charge, $3.5 million of which is due to a change in SAFS 121 concerning how to account for the present value of long-lived assets.</p>
<p>Earnings were restated to reflect acquisitions, it said.</p>
<p>Network Long Distance Inc.</p>
</text>
